Patch applied to EMLtoPST @ 6fe9025390a96fe0095457b56f12ce241ee4ba53 by
scripts/get_fixture_tools.sh. Regenerate with `git -C reference/EMLtoPST diff`
after editing the checkout; keep this preamble.

Why it exists: unpatched, the tool's output is refused by the upstream Rust
oracle at the store and table layers (see tests/fixtures/public/README.md,
`pstd-inline-cid.pst`), and it is not reproducible run to run. Each hunk is
either a [MS-PST] conformance fix or a default-preserving keyword parameter;
the CLI's behaviour is unchanged unless the new parameters are used.

  eml2pst/ltp/tc.py          TCINFO.rgib are END offsets of the 8/4-, 2-, 1-byte
                             groups and the CEB ([MS-PST] 2.3.4.1); the tool wrote
                             start offsets. Boolean cells are 1 byte, in the 1-byte
                             group ([MS-PST] 2.3.4.4.1); the tool wrote 4-byte cells.
                             HNID (variable-size) columns belong to the 4-byte group.
                             Upstream refuses with InvalidTableContextBitmaskOffset.
  eml2pst/messaging/store.py PR_IPM_WASTEBASKET_ENTRYID / PR_FINDER_ENTRYID (upstream
                             requires both: "Missing PidTagIpmWastebasketEntryId"),
                             a caller-supplied record key, a caller-chosen IPM subtree,
                             and a PR_VALID_FOLDER_MASK that reflects what was written.
  eml2pst/pst_file.py        threads those parameters through PSTFileBuilder.
  eml2pst/utils.py           filetime_now() honours SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH.
  eml2pst/eml_parser.py      a missing Subject header is an empty subject, not the
                             literal "(No Subject)" — the substitution hides the
                             empty-subject case the synthetic fixture exists to test.
                             RFC 2047 encoded words in Subject/From/To/Cc/Bcc are
                             decoded; compat32 returns them verbatim, so a non-Latin
                             subject would otherwise be stored as "=?utf-8?b?...?=".

